# Agent MCP Validation Rule

When working in this repository, a clean agent must follow this order:

0. Read `.cursor/skills/ngame-mcp/SKILL.md` when task touches MCP/gateway/scene status
1. Read `docs/agent-runbook.md`
2. Rebuild affected targets
3. Validate MCP behavior for changed runtime paths
4. Run `./scripts/validate.sh` unless explicitly waived by the user

## MCP minimum checks

- Use `world_snapshot` to confirm runtime state instead of inferring from logs alone
- Verify gateway fields (`upstream`, `ready`) when changing network/gateway logic
- Verify `view` + `render` fields when changing scene boot/switch/render flows

## Status and console expectations

- Keep status output readable (multiline when needed)
- Avoid always-on noisy panel diagnostics; print detailed state on explicit command

## Reporting expectations

- Report exact commands run
- Report what passed/failed
- If partial verification, call out missing checks and why they were skipped

